From 0d572443bc955d12812e8210d812326fb2d6f6c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y.z>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:25:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/21] dtb: discover a simple-framebuffer for the boot console

Prefer enabled /chosen children, fall back to any enabled node (vendor
trees reference cont_splash_mem from outside /chosen). Resolve the base
through memory-region before reg, convert the DT byte stride to pixels,
and accept only a8r8g8b8/x8r8g8b8. Properties are read raw so a malformed
node is rejected instead of panicking the parser this early in boot.

check_placement() refuses a buffer outside the bootloader's identity map,
over the kernel's own boot data, or in RAM the bootloader reported free
without a reserved-memory node claiming it.

Co-Authored-By: Cursor <noreply@cursor.com>
